# Technical Debt Tracker

This is a bounded follow-up tracker for discoveries that are real, useful, and outside the current Plan. It is not a general backlog, scheduler, task database, hidden journal, evidence archive, or second task system.

## Rules

- Record one concise item with an owner, source, reason it is out of scope, impact, proposed next boundary, and exit or acceptance condition.
- Link the active or completed Plan, decision, design, quality result, or incident that established the item.
- Keep uncertain findings Open and distinguish scanner observation from Confirmed project fact.
- Do not use this file to bypass Main's scope, acceptance, dependency, protected-path, or evidence decisions.
- Do not turn an item into work without Main creating or resuming exactly one matching active ordinary Markdown Plan.
- Remove or mark an item resolved only when the owning Plan records observable evidence; preserve the historical link.

## Entry template

```markdown
### TD-YYYY-NNN — short title

- **Owner:** named project or host owner
- **Source:** path, Plan, decision, check, or incident
- **Status:** Open | Proposed | accepted | resolved
- **Why out of scope:** bounded reason
- **Impact:** user, quality, security, operations, or maintenance effect
- **Next boundary:** the smallest future Plan or decision that could address it
- **Exit condition:** observable evidence required
```

